  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\n{展|てん} (spread, unfold) + {示|じ} (show, indicate).\n\nUSAGE:\n{展示|てんじ} is used both as a noun and as a する verb ({展示|てんじ}する). It is the standard term for putting things on display at museums, galleries, exhibitions, and trade shows. The related noun {展示会|てんじかい} specifically means an exhibition event or trade fair.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {展示|てんじ}する: to exhibit, to display\n- {展示|てんじ}{品|ひん}: exhibited item, display item\n- {展示|てんじ}ホール: exhibition hall\n- {常設|じょうせつ}{展示|てんじ}: permanent exhibition\n- {企画|きかく}{展示|てんじ}: special/planned exhibition",
